e_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.02800569084597815,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":28.8,"_gate_rev_durability":0.05940804395280974,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":54.7,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.03216418675291828,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":46.8,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.012111789615407265,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":65.1,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0002062694451924895,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":99.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.11732,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":78.2,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Hills Bancorporation operates as the bank holding company for Hills Bank and Trust Company that provides commercial banking in the state of Iowa. It accepts various deposits, such as demand, savings, and time deposits; and offers products, including real estate loans comprising residential, multi-family, and commercial real estate loans; mortgage and construction loans; commercial and financial loans; agricultural loans; and automobile, installment, and other consumer loans. The company also maintains night and safe deposit facilities; and provides collection, exchange, and other banking services. In addition, it administers estates, personal trusts, and pension plans; offers farm management, investment advisory, and custodial services for individuals, corporations, and nonprofit organizations; and originates mortgages that are sold in the secondary residential real estate market without mortgage servicing rights being retained. The company operates through its main office and its full-service branches in the Iowa counties of Johnson, Linn, and Washington. It serves individuals, businesses, governmental units, and institutional customers. The company was founded in 1904 and is headquartered in Hills, Iowa.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Lisa A. Shileny | President, CEO & Director | Age 48 | Compensation: $632,979 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 479 people. Revenue per employee of $364K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 5%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $136K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $75 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Hills Bancorporation is a small-cap financial services business with a $807M market cap on $175M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 7% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $65M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 37 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.14\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 12% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 1.7\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 14% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 65% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Hills Bancorporation (OTCMKTS:HBIA) Stock Falls 0.9% \u2013 Here\u2019s Why","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/hills-bancorporation-otcmktshbia-stock-falls-0-9-heres-why.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793845255.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.778,"tier":0,"scope":"company"